  "text": "It's eleven at night, and somebody just typed \"where is my order\" into the chat box on a small online store. The store has an answer for this. It bought one. The founder switched on the AI agent that came with the help desk, because that's what it was sold to handle. The agent reads the message. And hands it to a human. There is no human. There'll be one at nine. At the end of the month the help desk bills the store for every ticket the AI resolved. It's a short line. The founder is paying two people to answer \"where is my order,\" and paying a machine for the handful it did. Between the day that store bought the AI and the day it works, there's a job. I think one person can sell it, at a fixed price, to stores the vendor won't set up by hand. The strange part is who left the job undone.",
